WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.414
Pin input and result after a known-good run on your workflow.

00:00:03.444 --> 00:00:06.588
This example supplies synthetic invoice pins.

00:00:06.618 --> 00:00:13.825
Import the JSON, keep Read invoices as the fixture boundary, and
select Prepare notification as the output.

00:00:13.855 --> 00:00:15.504
Slack remains in the slice.

00:00:17.004 --> 00:00:19.520
Enable Stop after selected output.

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:25.797
The fixture replaces the Sheets input; the real Code node runs, and
this branch stops before Slack.

00:00:25.827 --> 00:00:28.324
Other reachable branches stay in the run.

00:00:28.354 --> 00:00:31.956
Review the two expected items, then download the local pack.

00:00:33.964 --> 00:00:35.261
Unzip the pack.

00:00:35.291 --> 00:00:37.919
Docker users can run the included script.

00:00:37.949 --> 00:00:43.520
This replay uses its case with installed n8n and n8n-check 0.1.8.

00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:45.969
The fixed Code keeps both invoices.

00:00:45.999 --> 00:00:50.458
A deliberate one-row regression fails the output check while n8n
succeeds.

00:00:50.488 --> 00:00:53.428
Both runs save JSON and JUnit reports.
